  "result": "Excellent! All 175 tests pass. I've added the VAT summary report:\n\n**vatSummary(invoices)** \u2014 Generates a VAT summary across all issued invoices:\n\n**Returns:** Array of VAT entries, each with:\n- `rate`: VAT rate (percentage, e.g., 21, 9, 0)\n- `base`: Sum of line amounts at this rate (after line discounts)\n- `vat`: Sum of VAT amounts at this rate\n- **Sorted by rate descending** (high to low: 21%, 9%, 0%)\n\n**Filtering:**\n- Only invoices with status 'issued', 'partially_paid', or 'paid' (excludes drafts)\n- Includes all line items from those invoices\n\n**Example:**\n```javascript\nconst invoices = [\n  issueInvoice(createInvoice({\n    customerId: 'C-001',\n    lines: [\n      { sku: 'DES-HOUR', qty: 10, discountPercent: 0 },      // 21% VAT\n      { sku: 'PRINT-A4', qty: 100, discountPercent: 0 }      // 9% VAT\n    ]\n  }).value, []).value\n];\n\nvatSummary(invoices)\n// Returns:\n// [\n//   { rate: 21, base: 85000, vat: 17850 },     // Design hours\n//   { rate: 9, base: 3700, vat: 333 }          // Printed flyers\n// ]\n```\n\n**Key features:**\n- Groups by VAT rate across all invoices\n- Accounts for line discounts when calculating base\n- Respects invoice status filtering (issued/partially paid/paid only)\n- Sorted high-to-low for reporting\n\n**Tests** (8 new) verify:\n- Basic VAT rate grouping\n- Multiple VAT rates in one invoice\n- Base calculation after discounts\n- Rate sorting (descending)\n- Paid invoice inclusion\n- Draft invoice exclusion\n- Empty list handling\n- Summing across multiple invoices",
